{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'for f in AGENTS.md ../AGENTS.md ../../AGENTS.md; do if [ -f \"$f\" ]; then printf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$f\"; cat \"$f\"; fi; done\nsed -n '\"'117,140p;1955,2045p' Makefile\nsed -n '1,175p' test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh\"","aggregated_output":"  readscaling vecscaling pipescaling chunkscaling printscaling complexity ioscaling hotscaling applyscaling zipmemory lazyscaling \\\n  devbootsmoke devirt directlink linkedrace mintgate ffi fibers fiberspoll fieldjoin fieldnum fieldread flarr fnform poolshape coreproc grenadine \\\n  gateboot gatebootsmoke gosm hasheq httpsfetch infer inferscaling inline inline-body irvalidate statlayout \\\n  jolt jolt-debug jolt-release joltsmoke libconformance libperf mandelbrot-num mathfl mvnhttp defmetacells staticsite gcpolicy stacklimit lazyretain \\\n  deadhost recordshadow emittedheads mirrordrift mirrordrift-regen regexdfacheck regexdfacheck-regen regexdfa regexanchor regexanchorprims regexanchorcheck regexsyntax regexbacktrack \\\n  hostarity enummodel enumregistrymodel cowpublishmodel doseqperf failfastmodel imagecoverage lazyshims narrow narrowhash numeric numwp oparity s64wrap pic protoret printperf remint sbperf sci selfhost shakelocal \\\n  traceemit tracecompilecost vfaslceiling \\\n  shakesmoke smoke sortedcoll staticnativesmoke stateimage test testbin transient unit unitcontext zlibregistersmoke zlibnativesmoke noexecsmoke \\\n  threadsafety maskedacquire ioerrno values wp ci\n\n# Only mark PHONY targets for names that have file system conflicts:\n.PHONY: nsaudit kondocheck build install test ci bionic-ci ci-shard ci-shard-list gate-run-test gate-run-ci gate-run-bionic-ci gate-run-ci-shard gate-status hooks attributioncheck noticecheck monitormodel \\\n<<<<<<< HEAD\n        gambitcheck gambitkernel gambiteval gambitsourceload gambitdaobytes gambityinrepl gambitdht gambityinequivalence gambitseed gambitweb gambitprofile \\\n=======\n        gambitcheck gambitkernel gambiteval gambitsourceload gambitdaobytes gambityinrepl gambitdht gambitdht-durable gambitseed gambitweb gambitprofile \\\n>>>>>>> gambit-ffi-p2\n        gambitgen gambitgencheck gambitseedcheck gambitunbound gambitunbound-regen \\\n        gambitffi gambitffi-abi gambitffi-errno-check gambitffi-load-failure-smoke gambitffi-bridge \\\n        gambitvars gambitvars-regen gambitstatics gambitstatics-regen gambittwins grenadinecheck \\\n        fibersbench dynbench \\\n        fibersresidue\n\ndefault:: build\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n# G2 kernel-test gate (jolt-mj95.4): the full booted manifest on native gsi,\n# driven through the real natives. Same detection-gated shape as gambitcheck;\n# a second on gsi. Run from the repo root (boot's irregex load is cwd-relative).\ngambitkernel:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 120 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/kernel-test.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n# G3 eval gate: real jolt source through jolt-compile-eval on the booted\n# manifest + cross-minted seed, renders pinned to Chez captures. Detection-\n# gated like gambitcheck. In the ci list: it is the only gate that runs\n# emitted code on gsi end to end, and while it sat outside ci every row failed\n# for two weeks (jolt-cw2p) with nothing red. Run from the repo root.\ngambiteval:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 180 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/eval-test.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n# The source-loader witness is self-contained. The full Yin gate reads a separate\n# datomworld checkout and stays opt-in while its native host closure is incomplete.\ngambitsourceload:\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" ]; then \\\n\t\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 240 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/source-loader-test.ss; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\nDATOMWORLD_ROOT ?= ../datomworld\ngambitdaobytes:\n\tsh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 240 \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" host/gambit/source-loader-test.ss \"$(abspath $(DATOMWORLD_ROOT))\"\n\n# The gates require the native startup. The equivalence gate runs both modes.\nGAMBIT_YIN_BOOT ?=\n<<<<<<< HEAD\nGAMBIT_YIN_CACHE ?= $(abspath build/gambit-yin)\ngambityinrepl gambitdht gambityinequivalence: export JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_CACHE = $(GAMBIT_YIN_CACHE)\ngambityinrepl gambitdht gambityinequivalence: export JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT = $(GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT)\ngambityinrepl gambitdht gambityinequivalence: gambitffi-bridge\n=======\ngambityinrepl gambitdht gambitdht-durable: gambitffi-bridge\n>>>>>>> gambit-ffi-p2\n\t@yin_root=\"$(abspath $(DATOMWORLD_ROOT))\"; \\\n\tif [ ! -f \"$$yin_root/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\" ]; then \\\n\t  echo \"$@: no Yin source entry under $$yin_root. Set DATOMWORLD_ROOT to a Datomworld checkout.\" >&2; \\\n\t  exit 2; \\\n\tfi; \\\n<<<<<<< HEAD\n\tcase \"$@\" in \\\n\t  gambitdht) JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_MODE=compiled sh test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" \"$$yin_root\" ;; \\\n\t  gambityinrepl) JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_MODE=compiled sh test/gambit/yin-repl-session.sh \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" \"$$yin_root\" ;; \\\n\t  gambityinequivalence) python3 test/gambit/yin-equivalence.py \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" \"$$yin_root\" ;; \\\n\tesac\n=======\n\tboot=\"$(GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT)\"; \\\n\tif [ -z \"$$boot\" ]; then \\\n\t  boot=$$(sh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 2400 python3 host/gambit/build-yin-boot.py \\\n\t    \"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" \"$(abspath build/gambit-yin)\") || exit $$?; \\\n\tfi; \\\n\tif [ \"$@\" = gambitdht ]; then \\\n\t  sh test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" \"$$yin_root\" \"$$boot\"; \\\n\telif [ \"$@\" = gambitdht-durable ]; then \\\n\t  python3 test/gambit/yin-dht-durable.py \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" \"$$yin_root\" \"$$boot\"; \\\n\telse \\\n\t  JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT=\"$$boot\" sh test/gambit/yin-repl-session.sh \\\n\t    \"$(GAMBIT_GSI)\" \"$$yin_root\" host/gambit/yin-repl-native.ss; \\\n\tfi\n>>>>>>> gambit-ffi-p2\n\n# Every Scheme global the full-profile boot references is defined — Gambit's\n# own linker report over the compiled boot, minus what the record translator\n# evals at runtime, against host/gambit/unbound-allowlist.txt (untaken paths;\n# a stale line fails). The boot splices most of host/chez, so a Chez-side name\n# reaching a shared file is otherwise an unbound global no Chez gate can see;\n# mirrordrift only compares names defined on BOTH hosts. It compiles the seed\n# to JS text; time varies by compiler build. Detection-gated. Ordered\n# after gambitboot: both regenerate boot-full.ss, and under -j a reader must\n# not open the file mid-rewrite.\ngambitunbound: gambitboot\n\t@if [ -x \"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" ]; then \\\n\t\tJOLT_GSC=\"$(GAMBIT_GSC)\" sh host/gambit/unbound-check.sh; \\\n\telse \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-SKIP); \\\n\tfi\n\n#!/bin/sh\n# Run the stock launcher and the same composition with a diagnostic host module.\n# Arguments are absolute paths. Build the qualified bridge first.\nset -eu\n\ngsi=$1\ndatomworld=$2\nmode=${3:-both}\ncase \"$mode\" in\n  */*)\n    # Older callers pass the kernel artifact before the optional corpus.\n    export JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT=\"$mode\"\n    mode=${4:-both}\n    ;;\nesac\nexport JOLT_TRACE_SOURCE=1\nrepo=$(CDPATH='' cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")/../..\" && pwd)\ncd \"$repo\"\nmkdir -p build/gambit-dht\nrun=${JOLT_YIN_DHT_RECEIPTS:-}\nif [ -z \"$run\" ]; then\n  run=$(mktemp -d \"$repo/build/gambit-dht/run.XXXXXX\")\nfi\necho \"gambitdht receipts: $run\"\n<<<<<<< HEAD\nmkdir -p \"$run/store\"\nexport JOLT_P1E_STORE=\"$run/store\"\n=======\n>>>>>>> gambit-ffi-p2\n\nsession() {\n  name=$1\n  launcher=$2\n  status=0\n  started=$(date +%s)\n  python3 test/gambit/yin-prompt-time.py \\\n    sh \"$repo/host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh\" \"${GAMBIT_DHT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:-5400}\" \\\n    \"$gsi\" \"$launcher\" \"$datomworld\" \\\n    --no-state --index-store dht: >\"$run/$name.stdout\" 2>\"$run/$name.stderr\" || status=$?\n  echo \"$status\" >\"$run/$name.status\"\n  cat \"$run/$name.stdout\"\n  echo \"$name launcher exit $status ($(($(date +%s) - started))s)\"\n  if [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]; then\n    tail -30 \"$run/$name.stderr\" >&2\n    return \"$status\"\n  fi\n}\n\nstock() {\n  session stock \"$repo/host/gambit/yin-repl-native.ss\" <<'FORMS'\n(+ 20 22)\n(quit)\nFORMS\n  grep -Fx 'yin> 42' \"$run/stock.stdout\" >/dev/null\n  grep -Fx 'yin> Bye' \"$run/stock.stdout\" >/dev/null\n  test \"$(grep -c '^yin> ' \"$run/stock.stdout\")\" -eq 2\n  if [ \"${JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_MODE:-auto}\" = source ]; then\n    grep -E 'ready dao[.]space[.]dht$' \"$run/stock.stderr\" >/dev/null\n  fi\n  echo \"gambitdht: PASS — stock launcher opened dht: and quit\"\n}\n\ndiagnostics() {\n  session diagnostics \"$repo/test/gambit/yin-dht-probe-main.ss\" <<'FORMS'\n(+ 20 22)\n(require 'p1e.probe)\n(p1e.probe/run :session-round-trip)\n(p1e.probe/run :memory-open)\n(p1e.probe/run :memory-put)\n(p1e.probe/run :memory-get)\n(p1e.probe/run :replicate-request)\n(p1e.probe/run :udp-loopback)\n(p1e.probe/run :udp-native-load)\n(p1e.probe/run :c4-control)\n(p1e.probe/run :close)\n(+ 40 3)\n(quit)\nFORMS\n\n  awk '\n    /^yin> 42$/ && step == 0 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\047p1e[.]probe$/ && step == 1 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\[ *:dht-index-put-get :segment\\/blake3-[0-9a-f]+ \\{:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3\\} *\\]$/ && step == 2 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :memory-dht-handle-opened$/ && step == 3 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :segment\\/blake3-[0-9a-f]+$/ && step == 4 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\{:p1e \"yin-dht-local-round-trip\", :count 3\\}$/ && step == 5 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> true$/ && step == 6 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> \\[ *:udp-loopback-ok \"Kv8A\" :closed *\\]$/ && step == 7 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :socket-native-loaded$/ && step == 8 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Error: .*blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target/ && step == 9 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> :closed$/ && step == 10 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> 43$/ && step == 11 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> Bye$/ && step == 12 { step++; next }\n    /^yin> / { unexpected = 1 }\n    END { exit !(step == 13 && !unexpected) }\n  ' \"$run/diagnostics.stdout\" || {\n    echo \"gambitdht: the probe did not produce the expected replies\" >&2\n    exit 1\n  }\n  echo \"gambitdht: PASS — selected DHT index put/get, portable replication request, UDP loopback and close, C4 refusal, clean quit\"\n}\n\ncase \"$mode\" in\n  stock) stock ;;\n  diagnostics) diagnostics ;;\n  both) stock; diagnostics ;;\n  *) echo \"usage: $0 GSI DATOMWORLD_ROOT [stock|diagnostics|both]\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\nesac\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' test/gambit/yin-dht-durable.py\nsed -n '1,220p' host/gambit/yin-repl-driver.ss\nrg -n 'JOLT_P1E_STORE|store|durable' test/gambit/fixtures/yin-dht-probe.jolt\nls -ld ../jolt-ffi-p2b/build/gambit* ~/.local/share/mise/installs/{gambit/4.9.8,chezscheme/10.4.1}\nrg --files ../datomworld/collab/jolt -g '*1795245000000*' -g '*p2*findings.md' | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' test/gambit/yin-dht-durable.py\nsed -n '1,220p' host/gambit/yin-repl-driver.ss\nrg -n 'JOLT_P1E_STORE|store|durable' test/gambit/fixtures/yin-dht-probe.jolt\nls -ld ../jolt-ffi-p2b/build/gambit* ~/.local/share/mise/installs/{gambit/4.9.8,chezscheme/10.4.1}\nrg --files ../datomworld/collab/jolt -g '*1795245000000*' -g '*p2*findings.md' | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Drive distinct Yin processes and assert persisted bytes and UDP replication.\"\"\"\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom contextlib import ExitStack\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport signal\nimport socket\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\n\n\nREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nTIMEOUT = int(os.environ.get(\"GAMBIT_DHT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS\", \"2400\"))\nADDRESS = r\":segment/blake3-[0-9a-f]{64}\"\nVALUE = r'\\{:p2 \"durable-gambit\", :count 7331\\}'\n# A transport event can take the prompt on the same tick as a reply.\nREPLIES = re.compile(\n    rf\"^(?:yin> )*('p2\\.probe|{ADDRESS}|{VALUE}|:missing|nil|\"\n    r\"'p2-(?:file|dht)-witness|7331|Bye|Error: .*?)\\n\", re.M\n)\nPROBE = \"(p2.probe/run :{})\\n\"\n\n\nclass Session:\n    def __init__(self, run, name, command, cwd, env, args):\n        self.name = name\n        self.out = run / f\"{name}.stdout\"\n        self.err = run / f\"{name}.stderr\"\n        self.deadline = time.monotonic() + TIMEOUT\n        with self.out.open(\"w\") as out, self.err.open(\"w\") as err:\n            self.process = subprocess.Popen(\n                [*command, *args], stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout=out, stderr=err,\n                cwd=cwd, env=env, text=True, start_new_session=True,\n            )\n        self.offset = 0\n\n    def __enter__(self):\n        return self\n\n    def __exit__(self, *_):\n        if self.process.poll() is None:\n            os.killpg(self.process.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n            self.process.wait()\n        self.process.stdin.close()\n\n    def send(self, text):\n        self.process.stdin.write(text)\n        self.process.stdin.flush()\n\n    def output(self):\n        return self.out.read_text(errors=\"replace\")\n\n    def await_output(self, pattern, deadline=None):\n        deadline = min(deadline or self.deadline, self.deadline)\n        while True:\n            match = re.search(pattern, self.output(), re.M)\n            if match:\n                return match\n            if self.process.poll() is not None or time.monotonic() >= deadline:\n                raise RuntimeError(f\"{self.name}: missing {pattern!r}; see {self.out} and {self.err}\")\n            time.sleep(0.2)\n\n    def reply(self, pattern):\n        self.await_output(r\"^yin> \")\n        while True:\n            replies = REPLIES.findall(self.output())\n            if len(replies) > self.offset:\n                reply = replies[self.offset]\n                self.offset += 1\n                if not re.fullmatch(pattern, reply):\n                    raise RuntimeError(f\"{self.name}: expected {pattern!r}, got {reply!r}\")\n                return reply\n            if self.process.poll() is not None or time.monotonic() >= self.deadline:\n                raise RuntimeError(f\"{self.name}: missing reply {pattern!r}; see {self.out} and {self.err}\")\n            time.sleep(0.2)\n\n    def probe(self, operation, expected):\n        self.send(PROBE.format(operation))\n        return self.reply(expected)\n\n    def status(self, expected):\n        status = self.process.wait(timeout=max(0.1, self.deadline - time.monotonic()))\n        if status != expected:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"{self.name}: exit {status}, expected {expected}; see {self.out} and {self.err}\")\n\n    def quit(self):\n        self.send(\"(quit)\\n\")\n        self.reply(\"Bye\")\n        self.status(0)\n\n    def require_probe(self):\n        self.send(\"(require 'p2.probe)\\n\")\n        self.reply(r\"'p2\\.probe\")\n\n\ndef reserve_ports():\n    # Reserve distinct loopback ports before launching the two UDP peers.\n    with ExitStack() as cleanup:\n        sockets = [cleanup.enter_context(socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM))\n                   for _ in range(2)]\n        for udp in sockets:\n            udp.bind((\"127.0.0.1\", 0))\n        return [udp.getsockname()[1] for udp in sockets]\n\n\ndef read_head(directory):\n    text = (directory / \"HEAD\").read_text()\n    match = re.search(ADDRESS, text)\n    if not match:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"{directory}: HEAD contains no manifest: {text!r}\")\n    return match[0]\n\n\ndef exercise(launch, run, kind, ports):\n    state_dir = run / f\"{kind}-state\"\n    directory = run / f\"{kind}-store\"\n    selected = f\"{kind}:{directory}\"\n    args = [\"--dir\", str(state_dir), \"--index-store\", selected]\n    with ExitStack() as cleanup:\n        peer = None\n        if kind == \"dht\":\n            source_port, peer_port = ports\n            peer = cleanup.enter_context(launch(\"dht-peer\", [\n                \"--no-state\", \"--index-store\", f\"dht:{run / 'peer-store'}\",\n                \"--dht-peer\", f\"127.0.0.1:{source_port}\", \"--dht-port\", str(peer_port),\n            ]))\n            args += [\"--dht-peer\", f\"127.0.0.1:{peer_port}\",\n                     \"--dht-port\", str(source_port), \"--dht-publish\"]\n\n        writer = cleanup.enter_context(launch(f\"{kind}-write\", args))\n        writer.require_probe()\n        if peer is not None:\n            peer.require_probe()\n            peer.probe(\"get\", \":missing\")\n        address = writer.probe(\"put\", ADDRESS)\n        writer.probe(\"get\", VALUE)\n        writer.send(f\"(def p2-{kind}-witness 7331)\\n\")\n        writer.reply(r\"(?:'p2-(?:file|dht)-witness|7331)\")\n        head = read_head(directory)\n        if selected not in (state_dir / \"state.edn\").read_text():\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"{kind}: state.edn failed to save {selected}\")\n\n        if kind == \"file\":\n            # A different spelling takes the same kernel lock. Keep the\n            # writer alive until the rival really reports the refusal.\n            alias = run / \"alias\"\n            alias.symlink_to(directory, target_is_directory=True)\n            rival = cleanup.enter_context(launch(\"file-rival\", [\n                \"--no-state\", \"--index-store\", f\"file:{alias}\",\n            ]))\n            rival.status(1)\n            rival.await_output(rf\"^{re.escape(str(alias))} is locked by another process$\")\n            if read_head(directory) != head:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"the refused launcher changed the writer's HEAD\")\n        else:\n            replication_deadline = time.monotonic() + 120\n            while True:\n                peer.send(PROBE.format(\"get\"))\n                answer = peer.reply(VALUE + r\"|:missing\")\n                if answer != \":missing\":\n                    break\n                if time.monotonic() >= replication_deadline:\n                    raise RuntimeError(\"replicated value never appeared in the second durable store\")\n                time.sleep(0.5)\n            peer.quit()\n            if not (run / \"peer-store\" / \"content.jing\").stat().st_size:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"the receiving peer left an empty content log\")\n\n        writer.quit()\n        # Compare after shutdown in case draining published a later HEAD.\n        head = read_head(directory)\n\n    with launch(f\"{kind}-restart\", [\"--dir\", str(state_dir)]) as reader:\n        reader.require_probe()\n        reader.await_output(rf\"^state: resumed from {re.escape(str(state_dir / 'state.edn'))} \")\n        reader.probe(\"recovered\", re.escape(head))\n        reader.probe(\"get\", VALUE)\n        reader.quit()\n    print(f\"{kind}: {address} survived restart with HEAD {head}\", flush=True)\n\n\ndef main(gsi, datomworld, boot):\n    receipts = REPO / \"build\" / \"gambit-dht-durable\"\n    receipts.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    run = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=receipts, prefix=\"run.\"))\n    print(f\"gambitdht-durable receipts: {run}\", flush=True)\n    overlay = run / \"jolt\"\n    yin = overlay / \"host\" / \"gambit\" / \"yin\"\n    shutil.copytree(REPO / \"host\" / \"gambit\" / \"yin\", yin)\n    with (yin / \"jolt\" / \"gambit\" / \"yin.jolt\").open(\"a\") as launcher:\n        launcher.write((REPO / \"test\" / \"gambit\" / \"fixtures\" / \"yin-durable.jolt\").read_text())\n    for name in (\"build\", \"stdlib\", \"jolt-core\"):\n        (overlay / name).symlink_to(REPO / name, target_is_directory=True)\n    env = dict(os.environ, JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT=str(Path(boot).resolve()), JOLT_TRACE_SOURCE=\"1\")\n    command = [gsi, REPO / \"host\" / \"gambit\" / \"yin-repl-native.ss\", datomworld]\n\n    def launch(name, args):\n        return Session(run, name, command, overlay, env, args)\n\n    ports = reserve_ports()\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=2) as pool:\n        results = [pool.submit(exercise, launch, run, kind, ports) for kind in (\"file\", \"dht\")]\n        for result in results:\n            result.result()\n    print(\"gambitdht-durable: PASS — persisted bytes and HEAD, state.edn resume, rival lock refusal, replicated peer bytes\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main(*sys.argv[1:])\n;; The native and interpreted boots use the same source loader and Yin owner.\n(##include \"host-apply.ss\")\n(##include \"source-loader.ss\")\n(##include \"unbound-vars-lib.ss\")\n(##include \"yin/blake3.ss\")\n(##include \"yin/file.ss\")\n\n;; Only startup uses these thunks. Every thunk initializes a namespace in the\n;; live loader's file/namespace context and can require another namespace.\n(define gambit-yin-compiled (make-table test: string=?))\n\n(define (gambit-yin-register! name file initialize)\n  (table-set! gambit-yin-compiled name (cons file initialize)))\n\n(define (gambit-yin-gensym-counters)\n  (list jolt-gensym-counter hc-sq-gensym-counter rdr-sq-gensym-counter))\n\n(define (gambit-yin-advance-gensyms! jolt syntax-quote reader)\n  (set! jolt-gensym-counter (+ jolt-gensym-counter jolt))\n  (set! hc-sq-gensym-counter (+ hc-sq-gensym-counter syntax-quote))\n  (set! rdr-sq-gensym-counter (+ rdr-sq-gensym-counter reader)))\n\n(define (gambit-yin-random-bytes size)\n  (let* ((n (jnum->exact size))\n         (out (make-u8vector n)))\n    (call-with-input-file \"/dev/urandom\"\n      (lambda (port)\n        (unless (= (read-subu8vector out 0 n port) n)\n          (error \"Gambit could not read OS entropy\"))))\n    out))\n\n;; A single outstanding request keeps the input reader from filling the\n;; mailbox. Only Yin's owner interprets submitted lines.\n(define (gambit-yin-wake)\n  ;; The owner is about to take live input. Session requires and eval use the\n  ;; normal source path, including macros and FFI declarations.\n  (set! gambit-yin-compiled #f)\n  (vector\n    (thread-start!\n      (make-thread\n        (lambda ()\n          (let loop ()\n            (let* ((owner (thread-receive))\n                   (line (read-line)))\n              (thread-send owner (if (eof-object? line) jolt-nil line))\n              (unless (eof-object? line) (loop)))))))\n    #f))\n\n(define (gambit-yin-close-wake! wake)\n  (thread-terminate! (vector-ref wake 0))\n  jolt-nil)\n\n(define (gambit-yin-wait-input! wake ms on-line)\n  (let ((seconds (/ ms 1000.0)))\n    (if (jolt-nil? on-line)\n        (thread-sleep! seconds)\n        (begin\n          (unless (vector-ref wake 1)\n            (thread-send (vector-ref wake 0) (current-thread))\n            (vector-set! wake 1 #t))\n          (let ((line (thread-receive seconds #f)))\n            (when line\n              (vector-set! wake 1 #f)\n              (jolt-invoke on-line line))))))\n  jolt-nil)\n\n(set! jolt-random-bytes gambit-yin-random-bytes)\n(register-class-statics! \"System\"\n  (list (cons \"currentTimeMillis\" gambit-epoch-ms)\n        (cons \"exit\" (lambda (status) (exit (jnum->exact status))))))\n\n(define (gambit-yin-run load-file after-load #!optional\n          (compiled-file (lambda (name file) #f)))\n  (let ((args (cdr (command-line))))\n    (unless (pair? args)\n      (display \"usage: yin-repl-main.ss DATOMWORLD_ROOT [Yin arguments...]\\n\" (current-error-port))\n      (exit 2))\n    (let ((root (path-expand (car args)))\n          (jolt-root (current-directory)))\n      (unless (file-exists? (path-expand \"src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\" root))\n        (fprintf (current-error-port) \"yin.repl: no source entry under ~a\\n\" root)\n        (exit 2))\n      ;; The builder canonicalizes the project root before it captures source\n      ;; locations. Use the same path for relative and symlinked launch roots.\n      (set! root (path-normalize root))\n      (with-exception-catcher\n        (lambda (e)\n          (let* ((value (jolt-unwrap-throw e))\n                 (message (jolt-throwable-message value))\n                 (location (jolt-current-source-string)))\n            (fprintf (current-error-port) \"yin.repl startup failed: ~a\\n\"\n                     (if (string? message) message (jolt-pr-readable value)))\n            (when (and (string? location) (not (string=? location \"\")))\n              (fprintf (current-error-port) \"Yin source: ~a\\n\" location))\n            (exit 1)))\n        (lambda ()\n          ;; Cache the qualified bridge before resolving Yin's paths relative to\n          ;; its own checkout. The source loader itself uses absolute roots.\n          (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'yin.repl)\n          (let ((load-ns\n                  (gambit-install-source-loader!\n                    (list (list (path-expand \"host/gambit/yin\" jolt-root) \".jolt\")\n                          (list (path-expand \"src/jolt\" root) \".jolt\" \".cljc\" \".clj\")\n                          (list (path-expand \"src/cljc\" root) \".cljc\" \".clj\")\n                          (list (path-expand \"src/clj\" root) \".clj\")\n                          (list (path-expand \"stdlib\" jolt-root) \".jolt\" \".cljc\" \".clj\")\n                          (list (path-expand \"jolt-core\" jolt-root) \".cljc\" \".clj\"))\n                    '(\"clojure.core\") load-file compiled-file)))\n            (parameterize ((current-directory root))\n              (let* ((audit? (getenv \"JOLT_YIN_AUDIT\" #f))\n                     (before (and audit? (unbound-var-names))))\n                (dynamic-wind\n                  (lambda () #f)\n                  (lambda () (load-ns \"jolt.gambit.yin\" #f))\n                  (lambda ()\n                    (when audit?\n                      (let ((added (filter (lambda (name) (not (member name before)))\n                                           (unbound-var-names))))\n                        (fprintf (current-error-port) \"yin source var audit: ~a newly unbound\\n\"\n                                 (length added))\n                        (for-each (lambda (name) (fprintf (current-error-port) \"  ~a\\n\" name))\n                                  added))))))\n              (after-load load-ns (cdr args)))))))))\n\n(define (gambit-yin-start load-ns args)\n  (def-var! \"yin.repl\" \"host-text\" (string-append \"Host: jolt / Gambit \" (system-version-string)))\n  (let ((main (var-deref \"jolt.gambit.yin\" \"-main\")))\n    (unless (procedure? main)\n      (error \"jolt.gambit.yin/-main did not load\"))\n    (apply jolt-invoke main args)))\n9:(def ^:private p1e-session-store (atom nil))\n28:        handle (p1e-call \"dao.jing.dht\" \"store-handle\"\n29:                         {:local (store/open :mem) :requests requests})]\n74:  (let [handle @p1e-session-store\n106:  (let [opened (open-store spec opts)]\n108:      (reset! p1e-session-store (:index-store opened)))\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 sto  staff   128 Nov 26 21:20 ../jolt-ffi-p2b/build/gambit-dht\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 17 sto  staff   544 Nov 26 21:19 ../jolt-ffi-p2b/build/gambit-ffi\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 14 sto  staff   448 Nov 26 21:13 ../jolt-ffi-p2b/build/gambit-yin\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 36 sto  staff  1152 Oct 19 19:37 /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/chezscheme/10.4.1\ndrwxr-xr-x@  8 sto  staff   256 Nov 18 00:24 /Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/gambit/4.9.8\n../datomworld/collab/jolt/1795245000000-engineer-p2final-consolidation.gpt-6.2-sol.stdout.log\n../datomworld/collab/jolt/1795250000000-engineer-p2b-compiled-session-boot.gpt-6.2-sol.findings.md\n../datomworld/collab/jolt/1795245000000-engineer-p2final-consolidation.prompt.md\n../datomworld/collab/jolt/1795254000000-reviewer-p2b-agyflash.gemini-3.8-flash.findings.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
