{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,230p' host/gambit/yin/jolt/gambit/yin.jolt\nsed -n '1,120p' host/gambit/yin/datomworld-launcher.patch\nsed -n '1,145p' test/gambit/yin-repl-session.sh\nsed -n '1,100p' ../datomworld/collab/jolt/1795245000000-engineer-p2final-consolidation.prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns jolt.gambit.yin\n  \"Yin's shared durable-store composition and Gambit's host modules.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.repl.main :as main]\n            [yin.repl.store :as store]\n            [yin.shell.main :as shell]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n(defn- activate-ffi [registry]\n  (module/register-host-module\n    registry 'jolt.ffi\n    {'sizeof ffi/sizeof}\n    {'sizeof (vm/primitive-profile 'sizeof :pure [1] #{} :none)}))\n\n(defn- materialize-sha256 [value]\n  (jing/materialize! (store/open :mem) value {:algorithm :sha256}))\n\n(defn- activate-store [registry]\n  (module/register-host-module\n    registry 'dao.jing.mem\n    {'materialize-sha256 materialize-sha256}\n    {'materialize-sha256\n     (vm/primitive-profile 'materialize-sha256 :pure [1] #{} :none)}))\n\n(def ^:private gambit-engine-inputs\n  {:host-modules {'jolt.ffi activate-ffi\n                  'dao.jing.mem activate-store}})\n\n(defn- open-memory-dht []\n  (let [join (requiring-resolve 'dao.space.dht/join)\n        payload-budget (requiring-resolve 'dao.space.dht/payload-budget)\n        local (store/open :mem)\n        node (try\n               (join {:local local})\n               (catch Throwable e\n                 (jing/close! local)\n                 (throw e)))\n        handle (:handle node)]\n    (try\n      {:index-store handle\n       :publication-policy {:max-payload-bytes (payload-budget node)}}\n      (catch Throwable e\n        (jing/close! handle)\n        (throw e)))))\n\n(defn- open-store [spec opts]\n  (let [opened (if (= spec :dht)\n                 (open-memory-dht)\n                 ((:open shell/composition) spec opts))]\n    (update-in opened [:engine-inputs :host-modules]\n               merge (:host-modules gambit-engine-inputs))))\n\n(defn- parse-store [arg]\n  (if (= arg \"dht:\") :dht ((:parse-store-arg shell/composition) arg)))\n\n(defn- parse-store-command [args]\n  (if (= [\"dht:\"] (vec args))\n    {:spec :dht :label \"dht:\" :opts {:index-store-spec :dht}}\n    ((:parse-store-command shell/composition) args)))\n\n(def ^:private composition\n  (assoc shell/composition\n         :composition-spec? (constantly true)\n         :parse-store-arg parse-store\n         :parse-store-command parse-store-command\n         :open open-store\n         :help-lines (into (:help-lines shell/composition)\n                           [\"\"\n                            \"Gambit also accepts dht: with memory backing.\"\n                            \"WebSocket serving and signed DHT names and heads are unavailable.\"])))\n\n(defn -main [& args]\n  (main/main! args composition))\ndiff --git a/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj b/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj\n--- a/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj\n+++ b/src/dev/yin_repl_launch.clj\n@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@\n\n\n (def ^:private gambit-capabilities\n-  \"Local --index-store mem session; no :yang/python frontend or WebSocket serving.\")\n+  \"--index-store mem, dht: (memory), file:<dir> and dht:<dir> (durable). No :yang/python frontend or WebSocket serving.\")\n\n\n (def ^:private gambit-blocking\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md b/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md\n@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@\n x86_64) is callable in-session. Evidence: `make gambityinrepl` in the jolt\n clone (both-platform PASS transcripts); the acceptance gate is\n `host/gambit/yin-repl-session.sh` — a 12-step ordered state machine over real\n-`yin>` replies. Yin args pass through (`--index-store mem`, etc.). Per-backend\n+`yin>` replies. Yin args pass through (`--index-store mem`, `file:<dir>`, `dht:` and `dht:<dir>`). Per-backend\n capability summary: JVM/Node/Dart = full (all frontends, all stores);\n `jolt-chez` = full minus native-parser availability as provisioned;\n `jolt-gambit` = core Yin (Clojure frontend, yin.vm, qualified FFI) with\n@@ -223,10 +223,9 @@\n   - `(use-store ...)` always executes on the local driver (even while attached to a remote server via `(connect ...)`) and is refused over remote `--port` evaluation requests (`Error: (use-store ...) is a local host command and cannot be run over a remote endpoint`).\n   - Like `(vm :type)` and `(trust ...)` / `(untrust ...)`, `(use-store ...)` never reads or writes `<node-dir>/state.edn`, so saved startup profiles are never clobbered by exploratory in-session store switches.\n\n-- **Gambit boundary (`jolt-gambit`, owner ruling C4):**\n-  - On `jolt-gambit`, `(use-store \"mem\")` (or `:mem`) on a quiesced session opens a fresh in-memory store and preserves the Gambit host modules (`jolt.ffi` and `dao.jing.mem`; re-require them in the rebuilt session before calling their exports).\n-  - Durable targets `(use-store \"file:<dir>\")` and `(use-store \"dht:<dir>\" ...)` hit the C4 blocking-FFI refusal inline during `open-first`:\n-    `Error: blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target — GC-safe blocking is unqualified on Gambit 4.9.8 (no verified release/claim transition)`\n-  - The active `:mem` store and REPL session survive the refusal intact.\n+- **Gambit stores (`jolt-gambit`):**\n+  - `mem` and `dht:` are memory-backed. `file:<dir>` and `dht:<dir>` use the durable directory store and resume from `state.edn`.\n+  - Store changes preserve the Gambit host modules (`jolt.ffi` and `dao.jing.mem`; re-require them in the rebuilt session).\n+  - The C4 refusal still applies to user-declared blocking FFI. WebSocket serving and signed DHT names and heads are unavailable on this host.\n\n ---\n#!/bin/sh\n# Drive the upstream Yin entry point. A shell exit status alone never passes.\nset -eu\n\ngsi=$1\nyin_root=$2\nlauncher=${3:-host/gambit/yin-repl-native.ss}\nmkdir -p build/gambit-yin\ntranscript=${JOLT_YIN_REPL_TRANSCRIPT:-}\nif [ -z \"$transcript\" ]; then\n  transcript=$(mktemp \"$PWD/build/gambit-yin/repl.XXXXXX\")\n  trap 'rm -f \"$transcript\"' EXIT\nfi\n\nstatus=0\npython3 test/gambit/yin-prompt-time.py \\\n  sh host/gambit/ffi/watchdog.sh 5400 \"$gsi\" \"$launcher\" \\\n  \"$yin_root\" --no-state --index-store mem >\"$transcript\" <<'FORMS' || status=$?\n(+ 1 2)\n((fn [x] (* x x)) 7)\n(def p1c-score 100)\n(+ p1c-score 1)\n(/ 1 0)\n(lang :yang/python)\n(require 'jolt.ffi)\n(jolt.ffi/sizeof :int32)\n(require 'dao.jing.mem)\n(dao.jing.mem/materialize-sha256 {:witness 1})\n(+ 21 22)\n(quit)\nFORMS\ncat \"$transcript\"\nif [ \"$status\" -ne 0 ]; then\n  echo \"gambityinrepl: a complete Yin session was not observed (status $status)\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# Each line must follow the previous one, with prompts on the actual replies.\nawk '\n  /^yin> 3$/ && step == 0 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> 49$/ && step == 1 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> 100$/ && step == 2 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> 101$/ && step == 3 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> Error: .*[Dd]ivid(e|ed) by zero/ && step == 4 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> Error: unavailable-parser: Yin REPL language :yang\\/python/ && step == 5 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> \\047jolt[.]ffi$/ && step == 6 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> 4$/ && step == 7 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> \\047dao[.]jing[.]mem$/ && step == 8 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> Error: .*blocking ffi is unsupported on the gambit target/ && step == 9 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> 43$/ && step == 10 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> Bye$/ && step == 11 { step++; next }\n  /^yin> / { unexpected = 1 }\n  END { exit !(step == 12 && !unexpected) }\n' \"$transcript\" || {\n  echo \"gambityinrepl: the Yin session did not produce the expected replies\" >&2\n  exit 1\n}\necho \"gambityinrepl: PASS — Yin state, evaluation error, frontend refusal, FFI, blocking refusal, and clean quit\"\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-26 16:36:48 GMT\nSession-ID: 01a2179b-8157-7a21-a433-adb815c465d5 (RESUME)\n# Task: P2-final consolidation — resolve the merge conflicts (union of compiled-boot + durable stores)\n\nRole: VM Runtime Engineer (consolidation round)\n\n## Situation\n\nTwo rounds you know are being consolidated: your compiled-session boot\n(gambit-ffi-p2b @ 4edb3460) and the durable Yin stores round (gambit-ffi-p2 @\n5c302a30, a different codex round) are merging into a consolidation branch\ngambit-ffi-p2-final @ /Users/sto/workspace/jolt-ffi-p2final (worktree exists,\nbranch off p2b). The merge has 2 unresolved conflicts — resolve them as the\nUNION (both feature sets live), not as one side winning:\n\n1. **Makefile:130** gate list — HEAD's list (with your compiled-boot targets\n   gambityinequivalence, etc.) UNION p2's `gambitdht-durable` (and any other\n   p2-only targets). Every target from both sides must exist.\n2. **Makefile:~1995** gambityinrepl/gambitdht/gambityinequivalence recipe —\n   HEAD's compiled-boot exports (JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_CACHE/JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT,\n   compiled mode) UNION p2's `gambitdht-durable` target and its\n   interpreted-fallback boot build. The durable gate must work, and the\n   compiled-boot targets must keep their cache exports.\n3. **test/gambit/yin-dht-probe.sh:25** — take the p2 side (the P1e-era\n   JOLT_P1E_STORE workaround is obsolete; p2 removed it because the durable\n   probe replaced that path).\n\n## Then verify the consolidated tree\n\n- make gambityinrepl (compiled boot, cache reused) — PASS, replies identical\n  to the interpreted reference\n- make gambitdht + make gambitdht-durable (p2's new target) — PASS\n- Stage-1 matrix: gambitffi, gambitcheck, gambitkernel, gambiteval,\n  gambitsourceload, seed/gen checks, emittedheads, deadhost — green\n- Commit the merge resolution.\n\n## Deliverable\n\nFindings appended: /Users/sto/workspa