s no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock, or namespace\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:5:   global.  It holds the one shell value a driver threads: the evaluator beside\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-6-   its separately-owned program media — `program-in`, which the macro\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:7:   expander observes, and `program-out`, which the evaluator's own observer\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-8-   watches (`docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md` §10.1) — the language, the value\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-9-   history, the output medium with its cursor, and a per-medium ledger\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-10-   recording the last outcome that medium answered.  Every function takes a\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-50-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-51-(def ingress-capacity\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-52-  \\\"Declared capacity of the composition-owned program medium, in elements.  The\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:53:   shell is the only appender and its one step owner serializes evaluation, so\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-54-   eviction can only follow a producer the composition does not make; a gap is\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:55:   therefore fatal to the current evaluation rather than a normal operating\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-56-   condition.\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-57-  4096)\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-58-\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-73-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-74-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-75-(def link-round-budget\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:76:  \\\"How many serve-and-run rounds one evaluation drives while its VM waits\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-77-   on a link (yin.vm.linker.md sections 6.3 and 7.2).  A round serves the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-78-   interpreter once and runs the VM once; a local content source answers\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-79-   within a few, so the budget is reached only by a link that stays\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-120-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-121-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-122-(def query-drive-budget\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:123:  \\\"The most `dao.space.query/q` calls one drive answers: one evaluation,\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-124-   or one re-check of a pending run.  A query is answered in the round\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-125-   it is asked, so without a bound a program that calls `q` without end\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-126-   would hold its input round in the drive forever.  Each call re-reads\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-131-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-132-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-133-(def query-call-limit-text\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:134:  (str \\\"the evaluation called dao.space.query/q more than \\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-135-       query-drive-budget\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-136-       \\\" times and was stopped (:yin.repl.query/call-limit)\\\"))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-137-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-138-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-139-(def vm-constructors\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:140:  \\\"The evaluators on `yin.vm`: the ast-walker, the semantic register VM,\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-141-   and the nameless de Bruijn stack and register kernels, each starting with an empty image.\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-142-  {:ast-walker ast-walker/create-vm\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-143-   :semantic semantic/create-vm\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-203-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-204-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-205-(def program-loaders\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:206:  \\\"The loader the evaluator observer hands each `program-out` value, per\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:207:   evaluator.  Every value there is one expanded canonical tree packet\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-208-   `[root rows]` (yin.vm.macro.md §2.4); each loader takes its row set — the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-209-   ast-walker through `vm-load-rows`, the semantic VM through\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-210-   `semantic/load-vector` over the v4 projection, and the de Bruijn\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-211-   kernels through A-derived stack and register images.\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:212:   No evaluator learns that an expander ran.\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-213-  {:ast-walker (fn [vm packet]\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-214-                 (ast-walker/vm-load-rows vm\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-215-                                          (macro/packet->row-set packet)\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-262-       \\\"  (repl-state)\\\\n\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-263-       \\\"  (help)\\\\n\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-264-       \\\"  (quit)\\\\n\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:265:       \\\"  *1, *2, *3  - last, second-to-last, and third-to-last evaluated\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-266-       \\\" values\\\"))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-267-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-268-\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-287-       \\\"built (yin.vm.telemetry, opt-in via the :telemetry {:stream ...} \\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-288-       \\\"construction option — yin.vm.telemetry.implementation-plan.md), but \\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-289-       \\\"composing a sink into this shell is not, so the command reports \\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:290:       \\\"rather than evaluates\\\"))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-291-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-292-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-293-(def ingress-loss-text\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-294-  (str \\\"One or more program batches were never observed from the program \\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:295:       \\\"medium; (reset) is required before more evaluation\\\"))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-296-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-297-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-298-(def result-loss-text\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:299:  \\\"the evaluation halted but its result never reached the output medium\\\")\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-300-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-301-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-302-;; =============================================================================\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-478-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-479-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-480-(defn- emit-result!\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:481:  \\\"Answer a halted evaluation's value on the output medium, after the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-482-   output it printed, so the shell reads results from the stream exactly as\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-483-   it reads prints.  The token carries `round`, so the shell accepts only\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-484-   this round's result.  Returns the append outcome, or `:untried` when\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-620-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-621-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-622-(defn make-vm\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:623:  \\\"Construct the shell's evaluator on `yin.vm`.\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-624-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-625-   The shell is the composition that chooses the VM's transport: the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:626:   evaluator is handed `:make-stream` bound to the ring buffer and the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-627-   `stream` module registered in its registry.  No telemetry stream is\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-628-   installed, and the VM owns no program medium: `make-session` builds the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-629-   medium, its attachment, the observer, and the VM together.\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-677-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-678-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-679-(defn- make-runner\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:680:  \\\"The run step the evaluator observer hands each loaded program: run the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-681-   VM through its protocol entry point, as a plain function so it can be\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-682-   handed to observer coordination on every host, and answer a halted\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-683-   run's value on `output-stream` under `round`.  The shell reads the value\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-740-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-741-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-742-(defn- make-session\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:743:  \\\"Build the evaluator, its media, their attachments and observers, the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:744:   expander, and the loader the evaluator observer feeds the VM, together.\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-745-   Reset and VM selection call this, so the whole composition is rebuilt as\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-746-   one and each attachment capability is bound exactly once per medium\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-747-   lifetime.\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-748-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:749:   Both evaluators sit behind the same two stages (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1):\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-750-   the expander observes `program-in` — `:program-stream`, watched by\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-751-   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:752:   `:row-stream`, watched independently by the evaluator's `:row-observer`,\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-753-   which loads each packet and runs it.  The code indexer's observer\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-754-   (`yin.repl.index`) is a peer attached to `program-out` beside it; the\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-755-   round advances each, and neither calls the other.  It records\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-863-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-864-   `:index-recovery` carries what the durable open recovered —\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-865-   `{:manifest <address or nil> :datoms <the validated snapshot or nil>}`\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:866:   — and the indexer is rehydrated from it here, before any evaluation\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-867-   is admitted (`yin.repl.index/rehydrate`): `q` answers the previous\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-868-   run's facts, which keep their own session tokens, while this process\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-869-   mints a new token for its own.  In durable mode `(reset)` and `(vm …)`\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1080-\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1081-(defn- commit-frontend\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1082-  \\\"Keep what a frontend program's lowering staged (`::frontend`, see\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1083:   `eval-compiled`) now that its VM state survives: the frontend session\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1084-   it leaves becomes the shell's `:frontend-session`.\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1085-  [state]\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1086-  (let [staged (::frontend state)]\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc-1088-      (contains? staged :session) (assoc :frontend-session (:session staged)))))\\nResults truncated to 150 lines (total: 2688). Use offset=150 to see more.\"}\n../jolt-ffi-p2/build/p2/datomworld/collab/yin-vm/1792141480000-architect-6d-plan-v2-mob-glm.glm-5-3.stdout.log:11:- **F1** (ready queue vs any-pc): **ANSWERED (v2 §3.1 `:ready` row, §3.2, §3.9 item 3(c))** — kernel order verified (`run-loop` active-first `engine.cljc:2211`/queue `:2216`; queue entries are the wait entry plus `:value :status :resource-updates :cursor` minus `:stream`, `engine.cljc:443-462`); resume reads `:resource-updates`/`:value` only, never the entry's `:cursor` (`engine.cljc:2299-2312`) — one mechanism defect inside the row's cell encoding found (my N1 below).\n../jolt-ffi-p2/build/p2/datomworld/collab/yin-vm/1792141480000-architect-6d-plan-v2-mob-glm.glm-5-3.stdout.log:15:- **F5** (all-pc stack equation false): **ANSWERED (v2 §3.5)** — every kernel citation exact: `stack-layouts` writes only parse-node pcs (`layout.cljc:118-131`), `:jump` is metadata not a child (`code.cljc:389-396`), terminators excluded (`code.cljc:413-414`), and the stack kernel behaves as claimed (`:const` pushes `:689-690`, `:push` only advances pc `:722-723`, tail call keeps `stack'` `:731`/`:747` without a frame `:737-738`, `:jump` `:777-778`, `:branch-false` pops `:780-784`, `:return`/`:halt` peek `:775`/`:787`); emitter order (`derive.cljc:92-97`) and allocator intervals over `live ∪ def` with `end < pc` expiry (`derive.cljc:127-130`, `:140-143`) verified.\n../jolt-ffi-p2/build/p2/datomworld/collab/yin-vm/1792141480000-architect-6d-plan-v2-mob-glm.glm-5-3.stdout.log:27:- **N5, P3 — halted-with-outstanding-wait (queue empty) is unspecified and untested.** Constructible (the F2 recipe run to halt instead of `run-fuel 1`); today's lift already classifies it `:blocked` and drops the halt result (wait-set checked before halted, `rows.cljc:1688-1691`), and v2's table preserves that — so no regression, but §3.1's \"the halt value is dead by the kernel's own order\" justification covers only the queued case (with an empty queue the machine is terminal and the result is observable via `vm/value`). Minimal fix: one sentence in §3.1 (\"halted with outstanding waits and an empty queue classifies `:blocked`; the halt value is dropped as today — pinned\") and one pinning test beside item 3(e).\n../jolt-ffi-p2/build/p2/datomworld/collab/orch-lane/1795400000000-architect-b2r3-confirm.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:5:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"pwd && rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g 'datom.world.md' -g '*oracle*' -g '*portable_harness*' -g '*prelude*' -g '*lower*' | head -60\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld\\nAGENTS.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793860000000-engineer-h3-1-fix-call-lowering.prompt.md\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793860000000-engineer-h3-1-fix-call-lowering.agy-gemini-4-argon.stdout.log\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791304928887-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10b-kernel-lift-lower.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791253000000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10-v1-lower.gpt-6-terra.stdout.log\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791304928887-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10b-kernel-lift-lower.dispatched.prompt.md\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791260000000-reviewer-d10-v1-lower-gate.prompt.md\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791304928887-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10b-kernel-lift-lower.findings.md\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791357500000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10b-b-kernel-lift-lower.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791304928887-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10b-kernel-lift-lower.prompt.md\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791260000000-reviewer-d10-v1-lower-gate.agy.stdout.log\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791253000000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10-v1-lower.findings.md\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791253000000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10-v1-lower.prompt.md\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791240000000-architect-d10-lower-inputs-ruling.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791357500000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d10b-b-kernel-lift-lower.prompt.md\\ncollab/yin-ucf/1791253000000-compiler-eng