ected output, the oracle\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs.cljc:5:   function, static-variable, warning and `@` groups and the P2 array groups\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/programs.cljc:857:   `[0]` columns are P2's and the object columns P4's.\\\"\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:3:Status: Designed 2026-10-17. Slices P1 and P2 (section 15) are implemented on\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:4:the `yang.php.antlr` route (P2: arrays, key coercion, `foreach` by value, the\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:137:#### 3.2.1 Reads, `isset`, `empty`, `unset` and builtins (P2)\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2022:| P2    | arrays: the value, key coercion, | the key-coercion fixture table;   |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2216:| C6 internal         | Engine: `sort`, `array_push`,       | restricted; P2   |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2287:| C15 iterator        | Engine: the exact outcome of        | restricted; P2   |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2294:|                     | in P2 or stay listed here           |                  |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2541:|                             | criteria 1 to 5 are direct fixtures (P1, P2    |\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:2562:  dependencies), five P2s (among them PHP semantics against the 8.3 oracle,\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.waitset.implementation-plan.md:620:| An answer that failed the outcome-map convention reached the classifier and woke with `:status nil` | An answer that fails `stream/validate-outcome`'s shape validation — a non-map, a missing or unqualified `:dao.stream/outcome`, a declared outcome missing its required keys — wakes as `:dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer`: terminal, out of `:waiting`, no `:advance` | \\\"An answer the library cannot interpret is terminal data, never an exception and never a wait\\\"; a `:status nil` wake is unnameable by any host branch. A well-formed outcome outside the declared set stays terminal under its own keyword, as before (W1 review, P2) |\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.waitset.implementation-plan.md:621:| A poll-time throw — a `:stream` resolved from a stale store record that fails its protocol, a defective transport — escaped `check` as a host dispatch error and voided the sweep | The per-entry poll is wrapped in a catch-all and the throw folds into `:dao.stream.waitset/invalid-answer`; the entry leaves `:waiting`, because an entry whose handle throws cannot be trusted to poll again | The engine let the throw escape; a library serving several consumers returns data instead, and re-parking such an entry would spin the sweep into the same throw every round (W1 review, P2) |\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.waitset.implementation-plan.md:622:| A resolver throw escaped the engine's sweep and voided it | Unchanged, now stated as the contract on resolvers: resolvers must not throw, and a throw voids the sweep — `check` does not return, and re-threading the previous waitset re-polls every entry, re-appending writers that already appended (`check` docstring) | Faithful to the engine. Catching around host resolver composition would hide host defects inside a diagnostic the library cannot ground; the no-dropped-state law is documented as the resolvers' obligation instead (W1 review, P2) |\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:246:  Outcome: no P0-P2; verdict \\\"ready to commit\\\". One P3 applied in the same\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:449:  the convention in the plan now so P2's pool observer needs no retrofit.\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:468:    50d48a71-9ff9-44b7-8dc0-b334e5f42aac | ready to commit, no P0-P2, three\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:545:    ready to commit\\\"; one P2 (the deletion/cleanup gap); confirmed the new\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:572:Next: **P2** — the pool, its two ends, and the in-memory backend — is the next\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:585:**P2 and P3 of docs/design/dao.jing.implementation-plan.md**, delegated and verified.\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:586:`glm-5.3` completed P2: rebuilding `dao.jing`'s observer over `dao.stream.observe/step`, migrating the pool's writer seams to v2, and successfully 