 (u/lam []\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3132:                            (app* 'php/release-cvs\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3133-                                  (args-vector (map #(u/v (symbol %)) cvs))\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3134-                                  (u/lit 0)\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3135-                                  (u/lit (count cvs)))))\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3136-               body)\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3137-        variadic? (boolean (some :variadic? params))\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3138-        fixed (remove :variadic? params)\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3139-        total (count fixed)\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3140-        required (inc (or (last (keep-indexed (fn [i p] (when-not (:default p) i)) fixed)) -1))\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3141-        bindings (concat\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3142-                   (map-indexed (fn [i p]\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3143-                                  [(symbol (:name p))\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3144-                                   (param-binding fctx n written required (= required total) i p)])\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3145-                                params)\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc-3146-                   (map (fn [c]\\\\\\\"}\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793502000000-architect-p4-heap-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:22:{\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tool_call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_f2ikmSNEXIeSnODOFinTftjp\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"docs/orchestrator-log.md:13192:Done: (1) T3 plan review returned from agy/gemini-4-argon (collab/1793008353000-reviewer-ts-t3-plan.gemini-4-argon.findings.md, session cf1b6797): verdict CHANGES - architecture and the Stage 0 split APPROVED; three P1 blockers with drop-in replacements (F1 the staticBlock subrule must not use a # label - ANTLR 4.13.2 error 153; F2 classExtendsClause needs typeGeneric? or generic heritage misparses; F3 the derived-constructor %thisc TDZ cell must thread into super.x/super.m/inner arrows) plus P2s (F5 eos on property declarations; F6 three missing T2 S1 helpers; F7 js/super-call five-step ordering; F8 delete expr.#x early error on any receiver). The reviewer pre-authorized folding the amendments directly into the engineer briefs without a second architectural round; the review is the amendment of record. The reviewer also verified both master states (local f5397a15 unpushed jolt lineage vs origin 40d56c72) - the plan's SHA citation was accurate for the local tip. (2) Stage 0 (T2 remainder) engineer dispatched on branch yang-ts-t2b (session d175441a, sonnet): the T3 plan's Stage 0 scope (constructibility by :kind + prototype/constructor pair, call/apply/bind, Object statics/prototype, Array constructor + Array.prototype methods, for-in/delete/in runtime) with the F1-F8 amendments BINDING, incl. F6's three missing T2 helpers. P3b's unblocked round (fixture enablement + S5 lowering) remains in flight (session c61cd179).\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13746:Done: (1) P4 S2's shiva verification caught six failures, all one cause: the e2e refusal list still demanded refusals for the three constructs S2 had just implemented (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\$a->b = 1, isset(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\$a->b), new A) - the engineer's local time-limit gap (the claude delegate's ~10-min background-shell ceiling on the laptop) left the stale expectations unseen. De-listed by the seat under the trivial-edit exemption (the pattern of three prior rounds); rerun fully green: 87 tests / 3041 assertions / 0 failures at 5bd34078. New brief convention: the round that implements a formerly-refused construct de-lists it in the same round. (2) T3 S2 landed (e632e9e2): make-function-nt (the engineer's additive deviation from the plan's literal 6-ary make-function ACCEPTED - identical semantics, avoids 45-site churn, recorded for the gate), constructor kinds/nt flow/bound construction, class_prelude_test 3/68 on four evaluators, goldens re-pinned. Shiva: cljstyle rc=0, focused green, Node subsystem 10 ns / 60 / 0 / pass. (3) Both S3 rounds dispatched: P4 S3 (finalization rows 48-51, clone row 52 + readonly 66-68, ctor-failed row 62, shutdown row 22, completing the flagged exception-ownership protocol, F3 + readonly fixtures :pending); T3 S3 (the class prelude: heritage, descriptors, private names + brand checks F4, super with the five-step ordering F7, define-accessor-half! wiring).\\\\\\\\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:13832:Done: (1) T3 S3 landed: the class prelude (heritage, private-name brand checks F4, super with the five-step ordering F7, receiver-aware super-get/set, derived completion rules, accessor halves; the S2 gap in construct-with-nt fixed; two signature deviations flagged for the reviewer). (2) The P5 plan of record received from fable (45KB, promoted): two load-bearing findings - the row-22 shutdown sequence splits between P4 and P5 behind a named phase seam (P4 is concurrently rewriting php/run-main), and NO yang.* guest has yet read/written a composition-supplied stream from prelude code, so P5's stream rulings are the precedent later slices copy; plus the php-cgi-not-php oracle ruling (the CLI SAPI has no superglobals and never warns headers-after-output). Its review dispatched to codex/luna (verify-the-claims brief). (3) The xlang demo resumed after the orchestrator prepped its worktree (the delegate had paused asking for mise trust/npm ci/gen:antlr - a brief-assembly miss: state prerequisites as done-conditions, not instructions, or do them first). (4) Seam compute DONE on shiva: the FULL permutation oracle recorded (1.77MB, corpus full rc=0); the phpt selection needs a php-src checkout on shiva (the runner wants <php-src-root> <tag>) - deferred as its own small task.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1983:  retention is accepted for C2; growth per yield is rejected (ruling 7).\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2374:Guest numeric `hash()` uses P = 2^61-1 on every host (ruling 7):\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2990:Host-export profiles (ruling 7). Publish refuses the prelude today: a\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3180:|      | manifests, enforced end to end (ruling 7). P2       |                 |\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:687:|               |                              | (ruling 7)                    |\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:1416:|       | tagged templates, Map, Set,      | suspension (ruling 7); Node       |\\\\\\\"}\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793502000000-architect-p4-heap-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:28:{\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"## Ruling: **(c), the measurement is wrong—not the assertion**\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe PHP fixture blocks **before module shutdown**. Consequently, `engine/collect` still traces the blocked main activation, its globals, continuation, and temporary/CV state in addition to the supplied generator reference. The `roots` argument contains **extra roots**, not replacement roots (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2541-2558`, `:2587-2597`).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThus 151 versus 5,596 cells measures different module-frame live sets, not growth owned by the suspended generator. There is no evidence here of a generator retention leak.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe last `$j` is not the essential problem: the blocker is after the caller loop, so its statement cleanup should already have run. The decisive error is comparing heaps while the entire caller/module activation remains live.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Required correction\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nPort the Python fixture’s measurement protocol (`test/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj:1228-1248`):\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Run the PHP program **to normal completion**, without injecting the blocker.\\\\\\\\n2. Preserve the suspended `h` through its deliberate `$it->self = $it` cycle.\\\\\\\\n3. Locate that one suspended generator in the final heap.\\\\\\\\n4. Call `engine/collect` with it as an extra root.\\\\\\\\n5. Assert equality of both cell count and deep content size at N=10 and N=1000.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAfter normal module exit, PHP’s CV and temporary cleanup must remove the caller’s ownership (`docs/design/yang.php.md:399-401`, `:673-676`, `:712-738`), leaving the cycle-rooted generator and its genuinely live delegation state. This is the same isolation strategy already used by the passing Python test.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### Generator semantics relied upon\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- A suspended generator legitimately retains its current frame, CVs, continuation, current/key, and delegate. Neither `$i` incrementing nor repeated `yield from` requires retaining every historical yield or caller.\\\\\\\\n- `%capture` may retain a fixed stale base; **growth per yield is explicitly rejected** by ruling 7 (`docs/design/yang.antlr.md:1971-1984`).\\\\\\\\n- Generator destruction releases CVs without running pending `finally` blocks; that does not justify per-iteration retention (`docs/design/yang.php.md:341-348`).\\\\\\\\n- Tracing follows continuation and closure payloads, so the existing deep-size measurement is appropriate.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Engineer round:** change only `live-after-collection` to use a final VM state, as Python does. Keep the N=10/N=1000 equality assertion unchanged. Do not change the generator runtime or cleanup code on the basis of this failing fixture. If the corrected fixture still grows, that result—not the current one—would justify a runtime leak investigation.\\\\\\\"}\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793510000000-architect-p4-heap-r2.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:5:{\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tool_call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_dxQqQZLbj1bzhGLJPR31Dn2V\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"300\\\\\\\\t- A closure made inside a method keeps that method's `$this` and called class;\\\\\\\\n301\\\\\\\\t  a `static` closure keeps neither. `bind`, `bindTo` and `call` replace `$this`\\\\\\\\n302\\\\\\\\t  and the scope class, and the closure's own `self`, `static::` and visibility\\\\\\\\n303\\\\\\\\t  checks follow the replaced scope (`bindTo($o)` without a scope leaves the\\\\\\\\n304\\\\\\\\t  scope alone, `call` binds both to the object). Callable forms\\\\\\\\n305\\\\\\\\t  (`[$object, 'm']`, `['Class', 'm']`, `'Class::m'`, invokable objects,\\\\\\\\n306\\\\\\\\t  `Closure::fromCallable`) resolve through the calling class scope.\\\\\\\\n307\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n308\\\\\\\\t### 3.8 Functions and the tables\\\\\\\\n309\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n310\\\\\\\\tThe function table and the class table are heap dicts in `php.rt/*`, populated\\\\\\\\n311\\\\\\\\tas declarations execute: top-level unconditional declarations are hoisted to\\\\\\\\n312\\\\\\\\tthe start of the unit as PHP does, and conditional ones execute in place. A\\\\\\\\n313\\\\\\\\tcall to an undefined function raises `Error(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Call to undefined function f()\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")`\\\\\\\\n314\\\\\\\\tat run time, before any argument runs (row 53). In addition the lowering emits\\\\\\\\n315\\\\\\\\ta warning-severity diagnostic `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` for a name in the\\\\\\\\n316\\\\\\\\tpinned PHP builtin catalogue (a checked-in list) that the prelude does not\\\\\\\\n317\\\\\\\\tsupply, so unsupported stdlib fails honestly before the program runs (law 12).\\\\\\\\n318\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n319\\\\\\\\t### 3.9 Exceptions, warnings and `@`\\\\\\\\n320\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n321\\\\\\\\t- `Throwable` with the `Exception` and `Error` hierarchies (`TypeError`,\\\\\\\\n322\\\\\\\\t  `ValueError`, `ArgumentCountError`, `ArithmeticError`,\\\\\\\\n323\\\\\\\\t  `DivisionByZeroError`, `UnhandledMatchError`, `JsonException`, the SPL\\\\\\\\n324\\\\\\\\t  exceptions); `try`/`catch` (multi-type `|`, optional variable)/`finally`;\\\\\\\\n325\\\\\\\\t  `throw` as an expression (8.0).\\\\\\\\n326\\\\\\\\t- **Warnings, notices and deprecations are not exceptions**: they are\\\\\\\\n327\\\\\\\\t  `:php.diag/warning` records appended to a guest-diagnostics stream the\\\\\\\\n328\\\\\\\\t  composition supplies (deterministic, since they derive from program state;\\\\\\\\n329\\\\\\\\t  owner decision B8.4), observable by `set_error_handler`, a guest callable in\\\\\\\\n330\\\\\\\\t  a cell invoked at the emission point by prelude code. `ErrorException`\\\\\\\\n331\\\\\\\\t  conversion is then user code.\\\\\\\\n332\\\\\\\\t- **`@`** lowers the expression's diagnostics with `error_reporting()`\\\\\\\\n333\\\\\\\\t  temporarily reduced to the PHP 8 mask (`E_ERROR | E_PARSE | E_CORE_ERROR |\\\\\\\\n334\\\\\\\\t  E_COMPILE_ERROR | E_USER_ERROR | E_RECOVERABLE_ERROR`). A handler installed\\\\\\\\n335\\\\\\\\t  by `set_error_handler` is **still invoked** and observes the reduced value;\\\\\\\\n336\\\\\\\\t  only the default output is silenced.\\\\\\\\n337\\\\\\\\t- `E_ERROR` fatals (undefined class, abstract instantiation) are `Error`\\\\\\\\n338\\\\\\\\t  throws. The uncaught-exception text is pinned to PHP's `PHP Fatal error:\\\\\\\\n339\\\\\\\\t  Uncaught ...` format without the file path.\\\\\\\\n340\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n341\\\\\\\\t### 3.10 Generators and iteration protocols\\\\\\\\n342\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n343\\\\\\\\t`yield`, `yield k => v`, `send`, `throw`, `getReturn` and `yield from` map\\\\\\\\n344\\\\\\\\tonto the landed C2 core (switch, yield-raw, exit, flag cells, a per-generator\\\\\\\\n345\\\\\\\\thandler stack); `Generator` implements `Iterator`. `foreach` drives arrays and\\\\\\\\n346\\\\\\\\t`Iterator`/`IteratorAggregate` objects; `ArrayAccess` and `Countable` are\\\\\\\\n347\\\\\\\\tsupported. Destroying a suspended generator releases its CVs but does not run\\\\\\\\n348\\\\\\\\tits pending `finally` blocks (corner C8, closed by P4-c).\\\\\\\\n349\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n350\\\\\\\\t### 3.11 Mixed HTML mode\\\\\\\\n351\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n352\\\\\\\\t`inlineHtml` tokens lower to `php/echo` of the literal text in source order\\\\\\\\n353\\\\\\\\tbetween code blocks. `?>` swallows one following newline (the lexer's rule,\\\\\\\\n354\\\\\\\\tpreserved through the span); the first `<?php` has no output before it unless\\\\\\\\n355\\\\\\\\tthere is text. Output order is statement order: exit criterion 1 is a direct\\\\\\\\n356\\\\\\\\tfixture.\\\\\\\\n357\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n358\\\\\\\\t### 3.12 eval\\\\\\\\n359\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n360\\\\\\\\t`eval` is a new compilation request (`yang.antlr.md` 8.6) sharing the caller's\\\\\\\\n361\\\\\\\\tscope, so it forces the dynamic-scope profile on its function. It is refused\\\\\\\\n362\\\\\\\\twith `:yang.php/unsupported :eval` until its slice (P9).\\\\\\\\n363\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n364\\\\\\\\t## 4. The reference, array and object lifecycle\\\\\\\\n365\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n366\\\\\\\\tPHP's observable aliasing (references, copy-on-write separation that unwraps\\\\\\\\n367\\\\\\\\tunshared references, destructor timing) is defined by the Zend engine's\\\\\\\\n368\\\\\\\\toperations, so this model is derived from them, not from an abstraction. Each\\\\\\\\n369\\\\\\\\trow names the Zend handler it maps to; each row is normative and is confirmed\\\\\\\\n370\\\\\\\\tagainst the pinned PHP CLI before the slice that claims it lands (the blocking\\\\\\\\n371\\\\\\\\trule, section 17.3).\\\\\\\\n372\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n373\\\\\\\\t### 4.1 What the engine does\\\\\\\\n374\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n375\\\\\\\\t- A **zval** is a typed slot in a CV, a hashtable bucket, a property table or\\\\\\\\n376\\\\\\\\t  a temporary. Refcounted kinds carry a header: strings, arrays\\\\\\\\n377\\\\\\\\t  (`zend_array`), objects, resources and references (`zend_reference\\\\\\\\n378\\\\\\\\t  {refcount, val}`).\\\\\\\\n379\\\\\\\\t- **Copying a zval** (`$b = $a`, `SEND_VAR`, `RETURN`, the `FE_RESET_R`\\\\\\\\n380\\\\\\\\t  temporary, array-literal elements) copies the slot and `GC_ADDREF`s the\\\\\\\\n381\\\\\\\\t  pointee: for an array, the **hashtable**, never its elements. Literal arrays\\\\\\\\n382\\\\\\\\t  are immutable and uncounted; the first write duplicates.\\\\\\\\n383\\\\\\\\t- **Writing into an array** goes through a write-address fetch (`FETCH_DIM_W`,\\\\\\\\n384\\\\\\\\t  `FETCH_OBJ_W`, `FETCH_DIM_RW`): the container is separated\\\\\\\\n385\\\\\\\\t  (`SEPARATE_ARRAY`, `zend_array_dup`) when its refcount is above 1, a missing\\\\\\\\n386\\\\\\\\t  key is auto-vivified, and the element's address is returned. `$a[k] = v`,\\\\\\\\n387\\\\\\\\t  `$r =& $a[k]`, a by-reference `f($a[k])`, `foreach ($a as &$v)` and `$a[] =\\\\\\\\n388\\\\\\\\t  v` all use this path, separating each level as reached.\\\\\\\\n389\\\\\\\\t- **`zend_array_dup`** copies buckets; a reference with refcount 1 whose value\\\\\\\"}\\\\ncollab/orch-lane/1793510000000-architect-p4-heap-r2.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log:6:{\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tool_call_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tool_HlwjJ17jpYMVdh9Uh5aRg4ce\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1272:                                     :destructed? false))))))]\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1279:    [php/released?\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1283:         (if (nil? c) false (= (get (cell/get c) :released?) true))))]\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1289:           (if (php/released? x)\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1297:           (if (php/released? x)\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1302:    [php/release-slots\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1312:               (php/release-slots tbl deps (+ i 1) n)))\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1315:     ;; the cell is marked released BEFORE its slots are, so a cycle back to it\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1316:     ;; (row 18) finds it released and stops\\\\\\\\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:1322:             (do (cell/set! c (assoc st :released? true))\\\\\