{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/gambit/fixtures/yin-durable.jolt\nsed -n '23,106p' ../datomworld/src/cljc/yin/shell/main.cljc\nsed -n '2140,2198p' Makefile\ntail -6 build/p2final/stage1.log\"","aggregated_output":"\n;; Appended by the process gate to observe the actual selected store.\n(def ^:private durable-test-opened (atom nil))\n(def ^:private durable-test-value {:p2 \"durable-gambit\" :count 7331})\n\n(defn- durable-test-run [operation]\n  (let [opened @durable-test-opened\n        handle (:index-store opened)\n        address (jing/segment-key durable-test-value)]\n    (case operation\n      :put (when (= :missing (jing/get handle address :missing))\n             (jing/materialize! handle durable-test-value))\n      :get (jing/get handle address :missing)\n      :recovered (get-in opened [:recovery :manifest]))))\n\n(defn- activate-durable-test [registry]\n  (module/register-host-module\n    registry 'p2.probe\n    {'run durable-test-run}\n    {'run (vm/primitive-profile 'run :pure [1] #{} :none)}))\n\n(defn- durable-test-open [spec opts]\n  (let [opened (open-store spec opts)]\n    (reset! durable-test-opened opened)\n    (assoc-in opened [:engine-inputs :host-modules 'p2.probe] activate-durable-test)))\n\n(defn -main [& args]\n  (main/main! args (assoc composition :open durable-test-open)))\n\n   This namespace owns no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock or namespace\n   global of its own: `composition` is one constant map of function values,\n   and each host's `-main` is a single call into the engine driver's `main!`.\"\n  (:require [yin.repl.main :as repl.main]\n            [yin.shell.cli :as cli]\n            [yin.shell.dht :as shell.dht]\n            [yin.shell.session :as shell.session]\n            [yin.shell.store :as shell.store]))\n\n\n(def composition\n  \"The plain-data bundle this project's hosts hand `yin.repl.main` as its\n   `:composition`: every key that driver documents, and nothing that reaches\n   past it.\n\n   The command-line half is `yin.shell.cli/hooks` — the flags, the\n   subcommands, the key file, the help and the banner text.  The rest is the\n   store and its transport lifecycle, each entry one function value taken\n   statically from the namespace that owns it, so the wiring is identical on\n   the JVM, on Node and on Dart and no host resolves a symbol at runtime\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 6 and 7).\n\n   The lifecycle functions all take the one composition session\n   `{:engine … :node … :key …}` and are driven by the engine driver's single\n   tick: `:step` advances the transport and answers its lines and its own\n   events, `:recheck-on-tick` serves the link and call media the engine\n   parks on and translates those events before they cross inward, and\n   `:stop!`/`:stopped?`/`:close!` are the one resource owner's exit — asked\n   once, completed by `:step`, and forced only by the drain's last resort.\"\n  (merge (cli/hooks)\n         {:composition-spec? shell.store/composition-spec?\n          :open shell.store/open\n          :close-store! shell.store/close!\n          :step shell.dht/step\n          :recheck-on-tick shell.session/recheck-on-tick\n          :recheck-after-input shell.session/recheck-after-input\n          :stop! shell.dht/stop!\n          :stopped? shell.dht/stopped?\n          :close! shell.dht/close!\n          :busy? shell.dht/busy?\n          :refusal shell.dht/refusal\n          :admitting? shell.dht/admitting?\n          :startup-lines shell.dht/follow-lines}))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :jolt nil\n   :clj\n   (defn -main\n     \"The shipped JVM entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n     [& args]\n     (repl.main/main! args composition)))\n\n\n#?(:jolt\n   (defn -main\n     \"The shipped jolt entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n     [& args]\n     (repl.main/main! args composition)))\n\n\n#?(:cljs\n   (defn -main\n     \"The shipped Node entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n     [& args]\n     (repl.main/main! args composition)))\n\n\n#?(:cljd\n   (do\n     (defn -main\n       \"The shipped Dart entry point: the engine's driver over `composition`.\"\n       [& args]\n       (repl.main/main! args composition))\n\n     (defn ^{:dart/name main} run-main\n       [args]\n       (apply -main args))))\n\n\n(defn startup\n  \"Parse the arguments and compose the shell with this project's\n   shipped storage composition.\"\ngambitffi-verify-digests:\n\t@sh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/verify-digests.sh \"$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)\"\n\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-bridge.scm \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/generated-shims.scm\n\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n\t@rm -f $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o[0-9]* \\\n\t       $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.c $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o \\\n\t       $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.scm\n\tcp $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-bridge.scm $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/generated-shims.scm $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/\n\tcd $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD) && sh ../../$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 120 $(GAMBIT_GSC) -dynamic -keep-temp -ld-options -pthread joltffi-bridge.scm\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1.sha256\n\t@cc --version > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/compiler.txt\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT_GSC) $(GAMBIT_GSI) \"$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)/include/gambit.h\" \\\n\t  \"$(GAMBIT_PREFIX)/lib/libgambit.a\" > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/runtime.sha256\n\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture.c \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt\n\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 $(GAMBIT-FFI-SHARED-FLAGS) -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture.c\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib.sha256\n\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt\n\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 $(GAMBIT-FFI-SHARED-FLAGS) -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-fixture2.c\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib.sha256\n\n# the present-but-unloadable candidate: a one-symbol dylib linked against a\n# dependency dylib this recipe then REMOVES, so dlopen fails with the loader's\n# own preserved reason (a missing dependency, not a missing file)\n$(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib: gambitffi-force $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/DIGESTS.txt \\\n\t\t$(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-dep.c $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-unloadable.c\n\t@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory gambitffi-verify-digests\n\t@mkdir -p $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 $(GAMBIT-FFI-SHARED-FLAGS) -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-dep.c\n\tsh $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/watchdog.sh 60 cc -O1 $(GAMBIT-FFI-SHARED-FLAGS) -o $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n\t  $(GAMBIT-FFI-DIR)/joltffi-unloadable.c $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n\trm $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-dep.dylib\n\t@shasum -a 256 $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib \\\n\t  > $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib.sha256\n\n# bridge + fixtures, always current: the entry every gambitffi gate depends on\n.PHONY: gambitffi-force gambitffi-verify-digests\ngambitffi-force:\n\ngambitffi-bridge: gambitffi-verify-digests $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/joltffi-bridge.o1 \\\n                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib \\\n                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-fixture2.dylib \\\n                  $(GAMBIT-FFI-BUILD)/libjoltffi-unloadable.dylib\n\n  ok     BLAKE3 known answer for 16384 bytes\ngambitsourceload: PASS — native source loading and compiler string emission\ngambitseedcheck: gambit seed is current with the sources\ngambitgencheck: records-gambit.ss is current with the records files\nmake: `emittedheads' is up to date.\nmake: `deadhost' is up to date.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
