{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"set -eu\ncat >build/p2final/findings-body.md <<'EOF'\n# P2-final — compiled Yin boot and durable Gambit stores\n\nThe merge combines \"'`gambit-ffi-p2b` at `4edb34606e0ffd5157027eba84df82d9ce3dc775` and `gambit-ffi-p2` at `5c302a301a9d4fab6da59bbf815f61cc1486edf2` on `gambit-ffi-p2-final`. Verification used Gambit 4.9.8 and Chez 10.4.1 on Darwin arm64 with Datomworld `bab7640f0b162444285ab622469de1abbefbb668`.\n\n## Resolutions\n\n- The `Makefile` phony list and recipes retain `gambityinrepl`, `gambitdht`, `gambityinequivalence`, and `gambitdht-durable`. The dry run resolved all four. REPL and memory DHT force compiled mode. Equivalence keeps both modes. `JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_CACHE` and `JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT` remain exported.\n- The durable gate builds or resolves the native kernel in the same cache and interprets its temporary fixture overlay. The stock memory probe drops `JOLT_P1E_STORE` and retains its compiled launcher, retained transcript, and stock and diagnostics entry points. The durable probe owns file and peer durability assertions.\n- The compiled-session cache now includes the Yin Scheme host sources, including the durable parent’s new `host/gambit/yin/file.ss`. A change to the file runtime invalidates the compiled session.\n- The inherited durable replication path calls `rand-int` to mint DHT query IDs. That reached Gambit `random-integer` with `1.0` through `rand`. The adapter now uses `random-real` for real bounds and keeps `random-integer` for exact-integer bounds. `gambiteval` checks the bounds for `rand` and the DHT query ID.\n\nThe new worktree initially lacked Gambit toolchain provenance and checked-out vendor submodules. The bridge check passed after recording provenance for the pinned installation. The Yin kernel prebuild and durable gate were retried after the Stage 1 dependency target populated the pinned submodules. The original source-reference build was restarted after the RNG correction so both compared launch modes use the final runtime.\nEOF\nrg -n '\"'\"'^#'\"' build/p2final/findings-body.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"set -eu\ncat >build/p2final/findings-body.md <<'EOF'\n# P2-final — compiled Yin boot and durable Gambit stores\n\nThe merge combines \"'`gambit-ffi-p2b` at `4edb34606e0ffd5157027eba84df82d9ce3dc775` and `gambit-ffi-p2` at `5c302a301a9d4fab6da59bbf815f61cc1486edf2` on `gambit-ffi-p2-final`. Verification used Gambit 4.9.8 and Chez 10.4.1 on Darwin arm64 with Datomworld `bab7640f0b162444285ab622469de1abbefbb668`.\n\n## Resolutions\n\n- The `Makefile` phony list and recipes retain `gambityinrepl`, `gambitdht`, `gambityinequivalence`, and `gambitdht-durable`. The dry run resolved all four. REPL and memory DHT force compiled mode. Equivalence keeps both modes. `JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_CACHE` and `JOLT_GAMBIT_YIN_BOOT` remain exported.\n- The durable gate builds or resolves the native kernel in the same cache and interprets its temporary fixture overlay. The stock memory probe drops `JOLT_P1E_STORE` and retains its compiled launcher, retained transcript, and stock and diagnostics entry points. The durable probe owns file and peer durability assertions.\n- The compiled-session cache now includes the Yin Scheme host sources, including the durable parent’s new `host/gambit/yin/file.ss`. A change to the file runtime invalidates the compiled session.\n- The inherited durable replication path calls `rand-int` to mint DHT query IDs. That reached Gambit `random-integer` with `1.0` through `rand`. The adapter now uses `random-real` for real bounds and keeps `random-integer` for exact-integer bounds. `gambiteval` checks the bounds for `rand` and the DHT query ID.\n\nThe new worktree initially lacked Gambit toolchain provenance and checked-out vendor submodules. The bridge check passed after recording provenance for the pinned installation. The Yin kernel prebuild and durable gate were retried after the Stage 1 dependency target populated the pinned submodules. The original source-reference build was restarted after the RNG correction so both compared launch modes use the final runtime.\nEOF\nrg -n '\"'\"'^#'\"' build/p2final/findings-body.md\"","aggregated_output":"1:# P2-final — compiled Yin boot and durable Gambit stores\n5:## Resolutions\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
