s) (hydrated session node) session)\n       lines\n       (into (vec events) head-events)])\n    [session [] []]))\n\n\n(defn refusal\n  \"The text that refused the composition's store after startup (a failed\n   bind or a hydration that could not complete), or nil.\n\n   `session` is the composition session this namespace's every function\n   takes — `{:engine … :node … :key …}`, `yin.shell.session/make`'s shape —\n   and the node is read off its `:node` key and nowhere else: one contract\n   for `step`, `stop!`, `stopped?`, `close!`, `busy?`, `follow-lines`,\n   `refusal` and `admitting?`, so a host cannot step one of them into\n   silence by storing the node under a name only another of them reads.\"\n  [session]\n  (get (:node session) ::refusal))\n\n\n(defn admitting?\n53:  (:require #?@(:jolt [[dao.stream.udp :as datagram.host]\n139:  #?(:jolt datagram.host/bind!\n148:  #?(:jolt (posix.random/rand-bytes n)\n226:     (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n261:        ;; The effective transport configuration, resolved once here and\n391:  \"The effective transport message bound `node` composes under: the most\n394:   that sizes anything against the transport reads the transport's own\n402:  \"The payload capability `node`'s transport declares: the most payload\n404:   the transport's own encoder and envelope (`dao.jing.dht/payload-budget`)\n408:   generic `:max-payload-bytes`, so the bound the transport enforces, the\n477:                    descriptor {:dao.stream/type datagram/transport-type\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
